#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:4
msgid "分子動力学法と統計アンサンブル"
msgstr "Molecular Dynamics and Statistical Ensembles"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:6
msgid ""
"分子動力学（molecular dynamics, MD）法は、原子に働く力から位置と速度の "
"時間変化を求める方法である。固定体積の気体の圧力を測る場合と、結晶が温度と ともに形を変える様子を追う場合では、一定に保つ量が異なる。"
msgstr ""
"Molecular dynamics (MD) uses the forces on atoms to calculate how their "
"positions and velocities change over time. The quantities you hold fixed "
"differ depending on whether you want to measure the pressure of a gas at "
"fixed volume or follow how a crystal changes shape with temperature."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:10
msgid ""
"古典力学の運動方程式と\\ :ref:`運動エネルギーと温度<temperature>`\\ を前提に、 "
"力から軌跡を求める方法、NVE・NVT・NPTで固定する量、平衡化後の測定区間の 見分け方を学ぶ。"
msgstr ""
"Building on the classical equations of motion and the relation between \\"
" :ref:`kinetic energy and temperature <temperature>`\\ , this article "
"explains how to calculate a trajectory from forces, which quantities stay"
" fixed in NVE, NVT, and NPT, and how to identify the production period "
"after equilibration."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:15
msgid "運動方程式と時間刻み"
msgstr "Equations of Motion and Time Step"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:17
msgid ""
"原子 :math:`i` の質量を :math:`m_i`、位置と速度を :math:`\\boldsymbol r_i` と "
":math:`\\boldsymbol v_i` とする。原子配置全体を :math:`\\boldsymbol R`、 "
"そのポテンシャルエネルギーを :math:`U(\\boldsymbol R)` と書く。セルを "
"固定し、外部とのエネルギー交換がない場合、力はエネルギーの勾配から求まる。"
msgstr ""
"For atom :math:`i`, let :math:`m_i` denote its mass and "
":math:`\\boldsymbol r_i` and :math:`\\boldsymbol v_i` its position and "
"velocity, respectively. Write the full atomic configuration as "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R` and its potential energy as :math:`U(\\boldsymbol "
"R)`. With a fixed cell and no energy exchange with the surroundings, the "
"forces follow from the energy gradient."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:22
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\nabla_i U(\\boldsymbol R),\\qquad\n"
"m_i\\dot{\\boldsymbol v}_i=\\boldsymbol F_i,\\qquad\n"
"\\dot{\\boldsymbol r}_i=\\boldsymbol v_i."
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\nabla_i U(\\boldsymbol R),\\qquad\n"
"m_i\\dot{\\boldsymbol v}_i=\\boldsymbol F_i,\\qquad\n"
"\\dot{\\boldsymbol r}_i=\\boldsymbol v_i."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:29
msgid ""
"初期の位置と速度を指定し、時間刻み :math:`\\Delta t` ごとに\\ :eq:`md-newton`\\ を "
"近似的に解く。速度Verlet法では、現在の力で速度を半ステップ進め、その速度で "
"位置を更新する。新しい配置で力を評価した後、速度の残り半分を進める [MdSwope1982]_。"
msgstr ""
"Given the initial positions and velocities, use a time step "
":math:`\\Delta t` to solve Equation \\ :eq:`md-newton`\\  approximately. "
"The velocity Verlet algorithm advances the velocities by half a step "
"using the current forces, then updates the positions using those "
"velocities. After evaluating the forces at the new configuration, it "
"advances the velocities by the remaining half step [MdSwope1982]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:33
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol v_i(t)+\\frac{\\Delta t}{2m_i}\\boldsymbol F_i(t),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol r_i(t+\\Delta t)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol r_i(t)+\\Delta t\\,\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2)\n"
"    +\\frac{\\Delta t}{2m_i}\\boldsymbol F_i(t+\\Delta t).\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol v_i(t)+\\frac{\\Delta t}{2m_i}\\boldsymbol F_i(t),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol r_i(t+\\Delta t)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol r_i(t)+\\Delta t\\,\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2),\\\\\n"
"\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t)\n"
"  &=\\boldsymbol v_i(t+\\Delta t/2)\n"
"    +\\frac{\\Delta t}{2m_i}\\boldsymbol F_i(t+\\Delta t).\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:46
msgid ""
"最初の2行から、位置の更新に初速度による移動と加速度による :math:`\\tfrac12(\\boldsymbol "
"F_i/m_i)\\Delta t^2` の補正が含まれることが分かる。 "
"この更新を繰り返して得る時系列を軌跡という。時間刻みが大きすぎると速い振動を "
"追えず、振動数や保存量に誤差が現れる。軽い原子を含む硬い結合は速く振動するため、 その運動を陽に扱う場合は細かい時間刻みを要する。"
msgstr ""
"The first two lines show that the position update combines the "
"displacement due to the initial velocity with the acceleration correction"
" :math:`\\tfrac12(\\boldsymbol F_i/m_i)\\Delta t^2`. Repeating the update"
" gives a time series called a trajectory. If the time step is too large "
"to resolve fast vibrations, errors appear in the frequencies and "
"conserved quantities. Stiff bonds involving light atoms vibrate rapidly, "
"so resolving their motion explicitly requires a small time step."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:57
msgid "|md-force-heading|"
msgstr "Calculating Forces on Atoms"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:59
msgid ""
"原子配置を更新するたびに、\\ :eq:`md-newton`\\ の力を新しい配置で評価する。 "
"力の求め方は、ポテンシャルエネルギーをどう与えるかで決まる。"
msgstr ""
"Each time you update the atomic configuration, evaluate the forces in "
"Equation \\ :eq:`md-newton`\\  at the new configuration. How you "
"calculate those forces depends on how you specify the potential energy."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:62
msgid ""
"**経験的ポテンシャル** では、原子間距離や結合角などの関数を定め、パラメータを "
"実験値や参照計算に合わせる。関数を評価するだけなので計算量は一般に小さい。 適用範囲は、関数の形とパラメータを調整した構造や組成で決まる。"
msgstr ""
"With an **empirical potential**, you specify a function of quantities "
"such as interatomic distances and bond angles and fit its parameters to "
"experimental values or reference calculations. Evaluating the function is"
" generally inexpensive. Its range of applicability depends on the "
"functional form and the structures and compositions used to fit the "
"parameters."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:66
msgid ""
"**第一原理分子動力学** （AIMD、FPMD）では、電子状態計算から力を求める。 Born–Oppenheimer "
"MD（BOMD）では、更新した原子核の配置ごとに電子の基底状態を求め、 "
"そのエネルギーから原子核に働く力を計算する。電子状態を反復計算するため、1ステップの負荷が "
"大きい。扱える現象と精度は、基底状態を使う近似と採用する電子状態計算の手法に依存する。 "
"Car–Parrinello法では、電子の波動関数を仮想質量を持つ自由度として原子核と同時に動かす。 "
"波動関数が基底状態の近くを保つように進めることで、各ステップで基底状態を解き直さずに 力を評価する [MdCarParrinello1985]_。"
msgstr ""
"**Ab initio molecular dynamics** (AIMD, FPMD) obtains forces from "
"electronic structure calculations. Born–Oppenheimer MD (BOMD) finds the "
"electronic ground state for each updated nuclear configuration and uses "
"its energy to calculate the forces on the nuclei. Solving for the "
"electronic state iteratively makes each step costly. The phenomena this "
"approach can describe and the accuracy it can achieve depend on the "
"ground-state approximation and the electronic structure method. "
"Car–Parrinello dynamics evolves the electronic wave functions alongside "
"the nuclei by treating them as degrees of freedom with a fictitious mass."
" Keeping the wave functions close to the ground state lets the method "
"evaluate the forces without solving for the ground state again at each "
"step [MdCarParrinello1985]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:74
msgid ""
"\\ :ref:`機械学習原子間ポテンシャル<mlip>`\\ （MLIP）では、参照計算のエネルギーや力を "
"学習したモデルから力を得る。電子状態の反復計算を学習済みモデルの評価に置き換えることで、 "
"同じ計算予算でも原子数を増やしたり、軌跡を延ばしたりできる。学習データで十分に表されていない "
"原子配置では、予測した力が参照計算からずれることがある。"
msgstr ""
"With \\ :ref:`machine-learning interatomic potentials <mlip>`\\  (MLIPs),"
" the forces come from a model trained on energies and forces from "
"reference calculations. Evaluating a trained model in place of iterative "
"electronic structure calculations allows more atoms or longer "
"trajectories for the same computational budget. For configurations poorly"
" represented in the training data, the predicted forces may differ from "
"the reference forces."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:82
msgid "NVE・NVT・NPTで固定する量"
msgstr "Quantities Held Fixed in NVE, NVT, and NPT"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:84
msgid ""
"統計アンサンブルとは、同じ巨視的条件にある系が取りうる微視的状態と、その 出現確率をまとめたものである。以下では :math:`N` "
"を粒子数、:math:`V` を体積、 :math:`E` を系の全エネルギー、:math:`T` を熱浴の温度、:math:`P` "
"を外圧とする。"
msgstr ""
"A statistical ensemble describes the microstates accessible to a system "
"under the same macroscopic conditions and the probability of each state. "
"Below, :math:`N` is the particle count, :math:`V` the volume, :math:`E` "
"the total energy of the system, :math:`T` the thermostat temperature, and"
" :math:`P` the external pressure."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:92
msgid "アンサンブル"
msgstr "Ensemble"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:93
msgid "固定する量"
msgstr "Quantities held fixed"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:94
msgid "主に揺らぐ量"
msgstr "Main fluctuating quantities"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:95
msgid "用途"
msgstr "Use"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:96
msgid "NVE（ミクロカノニカル）"
msgstr "NVE (microcanonical)"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:97
msgid "粒子数、体積、全エネルギー"
msgstr "Particle count, volume, total energy"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:98
msgid "運動エネルギー、瞬間の温度"
msgstr "Kinetic energy, instantaneous temperature"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:99
msgid "孤立系の運動"
msgstr "Motion of an isolated system"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:100
msgid "NVT（カノニカル）"
msgstr "NVT (canonical)"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:101
msgid "粒子数、体積、熱浴の温度"
msgstr "Particle count, volume, thermostat temperature"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:102
msgid "系のエネルギー、瞬間の温度、内部圧力"
msgstr "System energy, instantaneous temperature, internal pressure"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:103
msgid "指定体積での平均圧力"
msgstr "Average pressure at a specified volume"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:104
msgid "NPT（等温等圧）"
msgstr "NPT (isothermal-isobaric)"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:105
msgid "粒子数、熱浴の温度、外圧"
msgstr "Particle count, thermostat temperature, external pressure"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:106
msgid "体積、系のエネルギー、瞬間の温度、内部圧力"
msgstr "Volume, system energy, instantaneous temperature, internal pressure"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:107
msgid "外圧のもとでの平均体積や構造"
msgstr "Average volume or structure under external pressure"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:109
msgid ""
"NVEでは、運動エネルギー :math:`K` とポテンシャルエネルギー :math:`U` が "
"互いに変換されても、その和は連続時間の運動方程式で保存される。 :eq:`md-newton`\\ "
"を使うと、一方が増える速さと他方が減る速さが等しいと分かる。"
msgstr ""
"In NVE, the continuous-time equations of motion conserve the sum of "
"kinetic energy :math:`K` and potential energy :math:`U` as the two "
"interconvert. Equation :eq:`md-newton`\\  shows that one increases at the"
" same rate as the other decreases."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:113
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"E=K+U,\\qquad K=\\sum_i \\frac{m_i|\\boldsymbol v_i|^2}{2},\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{dE}{dt}=\\sum_i\\boldsymbol v_i\\cdot(\\boldsymbol F_i+\\nabla_i "
"U)=0."
msgstr ""
"E=K+U,\\qquad K=\\sum_i \\frac{m_i|\\boldsymbol v_i|^2}{2},\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{dE}{dt}=\\sum_i\\boldsymbol v_i\\cdot(\\boldsymbol F_i+\\nabla_i "
"U)=0."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:119
msgid "数値積分した軌跡では :math:`E` の小さな変動がありうる。時間とともに一方向へ ずれていく場合は、時間刻みや力の精度を見直す手がかりになる。"
msgstr ""
"In a numerically integrated trajectory, :math:`E` may fluctuate slightly."
" If it drifts in one direction over time, revisit the time step or the "
"accuracy of the forces."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:122
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"NVTでは、平衡での微視的状態の確率密度は相空間の標準的な体積要素に対して :math:`\\exp[-E/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]`"
" に比例する。:math:`k_{\\mathrm B}` は ボルツマン定数である。NPTでは体積も状態に含まれ、外圧との仕事に対応する "
":math:`PV` が加わる。体積と、その体積での物理的な位置・運動量に対する 確率密度は "
":math:`\\exp[-(E+PV)/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]` に比例する。 温度と外圧は、この平衡分布を定める条件である "
"[MdAndersen1980]_。"
msgstr ""
"In NVT at equilibrium, the probability density of a microstate with "
"respect to the standard volume element in phase space is proportional to "
":math:`\\exp[-E/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]`. Here :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}` is the "
"Boltzmann constant. In NPT, the volume is also part of the state, and the"
" term :math:`PV` accounts for work against the external pressure. The "
"probability density for the volume and the physical positions and momenta"
" at that volume is proportional to :math:`\\exp[-(E+PV)/(k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T)]`. The temperature and external pressure define this equilibrium "
"distribution [MdAndersen1980]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:132
msgid "熱浴と圧力浴"
msgstr "Thermostats and Barostats"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:134
msgid ""
"サーモスタットは熱浴とのエネルギー交換を、バロスタットは外圧のもとでの セルの変化を表すアルゴリズムである。古典的な系で運動の独立な自由度を "
":math:`f` とすると、瞬間の温度の推定量 :math:`T_{\\mathrm{kin}}` は"
msgstr ""
"A thermostat models energy exchange with a heat bath, and a barostat "
"models how the cell changes under external pressure. For a classical "
"system with :math:`f` independent degrees of freedom for motion, the "
"instantaneous temperature estimator :math:`T_{\\mathrm{kin}}` is given by"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:138
msgid ""
"\\langle K\\rangle=\\frac{f}{2}k_{\\mathrm B}T,\\qquad\n"
"T_{\\mathrm{kin}}(t)=\\frac{2K(t)}{f k_{\\mathrm B}}"
msgstr ""
"\\langle K\\rangle=\\frac{f}{2}k_{\\mathrm B}T,\\qquad\n"
"T_{\\mathrm{kin}}(t)=\\frac{2K(t)}{f k_{\\mathrm B}}"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:144
msgid ""
"である。重心運動を除いたり結合長を拘束したりする場合、:math:`f` から 対応する自由度を引く。熱平衡でも "
":math:`T_{\\mathrm{kin}}` は揺らぐ。 毎ステップの単純な速度スケーリングは :math:`K` を設定値に固定する。 "
"Berendsen法は :math:`K` を設定値へ徐々に近づけるので平衡化に使われるが、 "
"運動エネルギーの揺らぎを抑え、正準分布の分散を再現しない [MdBerendsen1984]_ [MdBussi2007]_。"
msgstr ""
"When removing center-of-mass motion or constraining bond lengths, "
"subtract the corresponding degrees of freedom from :math:`f`. Even at "
"thermal equilibrium, :math:`T_{\\mathrm{kin}}` fluctuates. Simple "
"velocity rescaling at every step fixes :math:`K` at its target value. The"
" Berendsen thermostat is used for equilibration because it gradually "
"brings :math:`K` toward its target. It suppresses kinetic energy "
"fluctuations, however, and fails to reproduce the variance of the "
"canonical distribution [MdBerendsen1984]_ [MdBussi2007]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:151
msgid ""
"正準分布のサンプリングには、揺らぎを保つ温度制御を使う。 Bussiらの確率的速度スケーリングは、平均を戻す効果に加え、正準分布に "
"必要な揺らぎを与える [MdBussi2007]_。Langevin法は摩擦と、それに見合う ランダムな力を組み合わせ、連続時間で正準分布を保つ "
"[MdLeimkuhler2013]_。 Nosé–Hoover法は補助変数を使う決定論的な方法で、 "
"正準分布を不変にする。軌跡がその分布を十分に訪れるかは系にも依存し、単純な 調和振動子ではNosé–Hoover法で訪れない領域が残ることがある "
"[MdHoover1985]_。"
msgstr ""
"To sample the canonical distribution, use a thermostat that preserves "
"fluctuations. In addition to restoring the mean, the stochastic velocity "
"rescaling method of Bussi et al. produces the fluctuations required by "
"the canonical distribution [MdBussi2007]_. Langevin dynamics combines "
"friction with a matching random force and preserves the canonical "
"distribution in continuous time [MdLeimkuhler2013]_. The Nosé–Hoover "
"thermostat is deterministic and uses auxiliary variables to make the "
"canonical distribution invariant. How well the trajectory explores that "
"distribution also depends on the system. For a simple harmonic "
"oscillator, some regions may remain unvisited under Nosé–Hoover dynamics "
"[MdHoover1985]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:159
msgid ""
"等方的な圧力制御ではセルの拡大・縮小で体積が変わる。結晶の軸比や角度が変わる "
"相転移を調べる場合は、その変形を許すセル自由度が要る。外圧が一定でも、 内部圧力とセルの大きさは揺らぐ [MdParrinello1981]_。"
msgstr ""
"With isotropic pressure control, the volume changes as the cell expands "
"or contracts. To study a phase transition that changes the crystal's "
"axial ratios or angles, the cell needs degrees of freedom that allow "
"those deformations. The internal pressure and cell size fluctuate even at"
" constant external pressure [MdParrinello1981]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:166
msgid "平衡化と測定区間"
msgstr "Equilibration and the Production Period"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:168
msgid ""
"初期条件の影響を減らすため、計算の始めに平衡化の区間を設ける。温度が先に 安定しても、密度や結晶の変形の緩和にはさらに時間がかかる場合がある。 "
"測定の開始時刻を決める際は、目的の量について平均や揺らぎが時間とともに 系統的に変わっていないかを見る。"
msgstr ""
"Begin with an equilibration period to reduce the influence of the initial"
" conditions. Even after the temperature stabilizes, the density or "
"crystal deformation may take longer to relax. To decide when to begin the"
" production period, check whether the mean or fluctuations of the "
"quantity of interest are still changing systematically over time."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:173
msgid ""
"平衡化後も時刻が近い観測値は互いに似通う。多数のフレームを保存しても、 独立な観測の数は同じ割合で増えない。軌跡をブロックに分け、ブロックの "
"長さを延ばしながら平均のばらつきを評価すると、時刻間の相関を無視して 不確かさを小さく見積もることを避けられる "
"[MdFlyvbjerg1989]_。"
msgstr ""
"Even after equilibration, observations close in time tend to be similar. "
"Saving more frames does not increase the number of independent "
"observations in the same proportion. In block averaging, divide the "
"trajectory into blocks and evaluate the spread of their means as you "
"increase the block length. This helps avoid underestimating uncertainty "
"by ignoring correlations between times [MdFlyvbjerg1989]_."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:181
msgid "計算事例での使い分け"
msgstr "Choosing a Method in the Calculation Examples"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:183
msgid ""
"`気体のモル体積 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.html>`__ "
"では、温度と体積を指定して平均圧力を求める。熱浴を使うNVTでは、圧力が応答となる。"
msgstr ""
"In `Molar Volume of a Gas <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/gas_laws/argon_molar_volume.html>`__, the temperature"
" and volume are specified to obtain the average pressure. Under NVT, with"
" a thermostat, the pressure is the response."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:185
msgid ""
"`CO₂の赤外スペクトル <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/co2_ir/ir_spectrum.html>`__ "
"では、熱浴を外したNVEの軌跡から分子振動を読み取る。熱浴による運動の変化を 避け、初速度で与えたエネルギーが振動としてどう現れるかを調べる。"
msgstr ""
"In `Infrared Spectrum of CO₂ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/co2_ir/ir_spectrum.html>`__, molecular vibrations are"
" extracted from an NVE trajectory with the thermostat off. This avoids "
"altering the motion with the thermostat and shows how the energy imparted"
" by the initial velocities appears as vibrations."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:188
msgid ""
"`BaTiO₃の構造相転移 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html>`__ "
"では、圧力を制御しながら熱浴の目標温度を上げ、セルと原子配置の変化を追う。 NPTの制御を使っているが、温度は時間とともに変わる。各温度での平衡を"
" 評価するには、保持時間と構造の緩和を考慮する。"
msgstr ""
"In `Structural Phase Transitions in BaTiO₃ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/phase_transition.html>`__, the thermostat "
"target temperature rises under pressure control as the cell and atomic "
"configuration evolve. The simulation uses NPT control, but the "
"temperature changes over time. Evaluating equilibrium at each temperature"
" requires accounting for the hold time and structural relaxation."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:196
msgid "説明用の事例：時間刻みと振動子"
msgstr "Worked Example: Time Step and a Harmonic Oscillator"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:198
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"時間刻みを選ぶ目安は、追いたい最速の振動を1周期あたり何回更新できるかである。 1次元調和振動子 :math:`m\\ddot "
"x=-m\\omega^2x` を、初期変位 :math:`x_0`、 初速度ゼロから\\ :eq:`md-velocity-verlet`\\ "
"で進める。厳密な周期を :math:`\\tau_{\\rm osc}=2\\pi/\\omega` とする。"
msgstr ""
"A guideline for choosing the time step is the number of updates per "
"period of the fastest vibration you want to resolve. Start the one-"
"dimensional harmonic oscillator :math:`m\\ddot x=-m\\omega^2x` at "
"displacement :math:`x_0` with zero initial velocity and integrate it "
"using Equation \\ :eq:`md-velocity-verlet`\\ . Let :math:`\\tau_{\\rm "
"osc}=2\\pi/\\omega` be the exact period."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:203
msgid ""
":math:`h=\\omega\\Delta t`、:math:`X=x/x_0`、:math:`W=v/(\\omega x_0)` "
"とおく。半ステップの速度を位置の式へ代入し、更新後の位置を使って速度を求めると、 次の時刻の :math:`(X',W')` は"
msgstr ""
"Set :math:`h=\\omega\\Delta t`, :math:`X=x/x_0`, and :math:`W=v/(\\omega "
"x_0)`. Substituting the half-step velocity into the position equation and"
" using the updated position to calculate the velocity gives the next "
"state :math:`(X',W')`:"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:207
msgid ""
"X'=(1-h^2/2)X+hW,\\qquad\n"
"W'=(1-h^2/2)W-h(1-h^2/4)X"
msgstr ""
"X'=(1-h^2/2)X+hW,\\qquad\n"
"W'=(1-h^2/2)W-h(1-h^2/4)X"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:213
msgid ""
"である。この更新で :math:`W^2+(1-h^2/4)X^2` は保存される。 :math:`0<h<2` "
"では軌道が有界で、1ステップあたりの位相の進みは :math:`\\arccos(1-h^2/2)` になる。全エネルギーを初期値 "
":math:`E_0=m\\omega^2x_0^2/2` で割ると :math:`X^2+W^2` なので、 この初期条件では "
":math:`(E-E_0)/E_0=(h^2/4)(X^2-1)` である。 全エネルギーの変動幅は時間刻みの二乗に比例する。"
msgstr ""
"This update conserves :math:`W^2+(1-h^2/4)X^2`. When :math:`0<h<2`, the "
"orbit is bounded and the phase advances by :math:`\\arccos(1-h^2/2)` per "
"step. Dividing the total energy by its initial value "
":math:`E_0=m\\omega^2x_0^2/2` gives :math:`X^2+W^2`. For these initial "
"conditions, :math:`(E-E_0)/E_0=(h^2/4)(X^2-1)`. The amplitude of the "
"total energy fluctuations is proportional to the square of the time step."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:220
msgid "厳密な周期を分割して10周期ぶん積分した結果"
msgstr ""
"Results of integrating over 10 exact periods with different numbers of "
"steps per period."

