#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:238
msgid ""
"この振動子では1周期を20分割しても、エネルギーは最大約2.5%ずれる。 :numref:`fig-md-verlet-step`\\ "
"では、刻みが粗いと変動幅が広がる。 数値的な周期も短くなるため、変動幅に加えて、観測したい振動数の変化も 刻み選びの手がかりになる。"
msgstr ""
"Even with 20 steps per period, the energy in this oscillator deviates by "
"up to about 2.5%. In :numref:`fig-md-verlet-step`\\ , the deviations grow"
" as the time step increases. The numerical period also shortens, so "
"consider both the amplitude of the deviations and the change in the "
"frequency of interest when choosing the time step."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:243
msgid "周期を50、20、10分割したときの相対エネルギーの時系列。10分割が最も大きく変動する。"
msgstr ""
"Relative energy deviation over time for 50, 20, and 10 steps per period. "
"The fluctuations are largest with 10 steps per period."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:248
msgid "はじめの3周期での全エネルギーのずれ。横軸は厳密な周期で割った時刻。 実線、破線、一点鎖線は1周期あたり50、20、10ステップを表す。"
msgstr ""
"Deviation in total energy over the first three periods. The horizontal "
"axis gives time divided by the exact period. The solid, dashed, and dash-"
"dot lines show 50, 20, and 10 steps per period, respectively."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:254
msgid "説明用の事例：粒子数による温度の揺らぎ"
msgstr "Worked Example: Temperature Fluctuations and Particle Count"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:256
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"正準分布では、温度制御が適切でも、小さい系ほど瞬間の温度が大きく揺らぐ。 独立な二次形式の運動自由度が :math:`f` "
"個あるとき、各項の平均は :math:`k_{\\rm B}T/2`、分散は :math:`(k_{\\rm B}T)^2/2` である。 "
"分散を足し、:eq:`md-kinetic-temperature`\\ で温度に換算してから平均で割る。"
msgstr ""
"In the canonical distribution, the instantaneous temperature fluctuates "
"more in smaller systems, even with appropriate temperature control. If "
"there are :math:`f` independent quadratic degrees of freedom for motion, "
"each term has mean :math:`k_{\\rm B}T/2` and variance :math:`(k_{\\rm "
"B}T)^2/2`. Add the variances, convert to temperature using Equation :eq"
":`md-kinetic-temperature`\\ , and divide the resulting standard deviation"
" by the mean:"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:261
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\operatorname{SD}(T_{\\rm kin})}{T}\n"
"=\\frac{\\sqrt{f(k_{\\rm B}T)^2/2}}{f k_{\\rm B}T/2}\n"
"=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{f}}."
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\\operatorname{SD}(T_{\\rm kin})}{T}\n"
"=\\frac{\\sqrt{f(k_{\\rm B}T)^2/2}}{f k_{\\rm B}T/2}\n"
"=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{f}}."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:268
msgid ""
"3次元で重心運動だけを除くなら :math:`f=3N-3` となる。:math:`N=32,256,2048` "
"に対する相対標準偏差は、順に14.66%、5.11%、1.80%である。 全自由度を数える場合の導出は\\ "
":ref:`温度の計算<temperature>`\\ にある。 軌跡の平均温度の標準誤差には、瞬間値の揺らぎに加えて時刻間の相関も効く。"
msgstr ""
"In three dimensions, if only center-of-mass motion is removed, "
":math:`f=3N-3`. For :math:`N=32,256,2048`, the relative standard "
"deviations are 14.66%, 5.11%, and 1.80%, respectively. See the derivation"
" counting all degrees of freedom in the article on \\ :ref:`calculating "
"temperature <temperature>`\\ . The standard error of the trajectory's "
"mean temperature depends on correlations between times as well as on the "
"instantaneous temperature fluctuations."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:276
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:278
msgid ""
"**刻みの収束。** 調和振動子の変動幅は一つの振動と積分法から得た目安である。 "
"実際の系は速い衝突や拘束、電子状態の数値誤差も含む。刻みを半分にして、 エネルギーの一方向のずれと、目的の振動数や圧力の両方が変わるかを見る。"
msgstr ""
"**Time step convergence.** The amplitude of the harmonic oscillator's "
"energy fluctuations is a guideline based on one vibration and one "
"integration method. Real systems may also involve fast collisions, "
"constraints, and numerical errors in the electronic structure "
"calculation. Halve the time step and check for changes in both the one-"
"directional energy drift and the observable of interest, such as "
"frequency or pressure."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:281
msgid ""
"**平衡分布と時間相関。** 正準分布を再現するサーモスタットでも、摩擦や 温度調整は軌跡の時間相関を変えうる。振動スペクトルと平衡平均では、 "
"同じ温度制御が適切かを別々に判断する。"
msgstr ""
"**Equilibrium distributions and time correlations.** Even with a "
"thermostat that reproduces the canonical distribution, friction or "
"temperature adjustments can alter the time correlations in the "
"trajectory. Assess separately whether the same thermostat is suitable for"
" vibrational spectra and for equilibrium averages."

#: ../../md/ensembles.rst:284
msgid ""
"**観測時間。** 温度の揺らぎが理論値に近い場合でも、相の切り替わりなど 遅い過程を観測できたかは別に評価する。初期構造を変えた軌跡を比べると、"
" 一つの構造にとどまったために平均が安定して見える場合を見分けられる。"
msgstr ""
"**Observation time.** Even if the temperature fluctuations are close to "
"the theoretical value, assess separately whether slow processes such as "
"switching between phases have been observed. Comparing trajectories that "
"start from different structures can reveal when an average appears stable"
" because the system stayed in a single structure."

